WEBVTT

1
00:00:36.650 --> 00:00:38.330
Hello, Maedeh.

2
00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:41.890
Sorry to drag you here.

3
00:00:42.490 --> 00:00:43.850
You're really

4
00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:46.050
my best friend.

5
00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:49.050
The only one I trust.

6
00:00:51.930 --> 00:00:53.610
Forward this message

7
00:00:53.770 --> 00:00:56.050
to Behnaz Jafari.

8
00:00:56.730 --> 00:00:57.970
Please.

9
00:01:00.570 --> 00:01:02.050
It's really urgent.

10
00:01:12.850 --> 00:01:14.810
Hello, Madam Jafari.

11
00:01:18.250 --> 00:01:19.850
I'm Marziyeh Rezaei.

12
00:01:20.010 --> 00:01:21.730
From Saran village.

13
00:01:22.090 --> 00:01:24.050
Near Mianeh.

14
00:01:31.250 --> 00:01:32.730
I don't know...

15
00:01:32.890 --> 00:01:35.050
I don't know how to say this.

16
00:01:36.730 --> 00:01:39.010
I can't think.

17
00:01:43.610 --> 00:01:46.010
I've loved cinema
since I was little.

18
00:01:47.050 --> 00:01:50.210
I've always dreamed
of being an actress.

19
00:01:50.890 --> 00:01:52.770
I fought for that.

20
00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:56.090
I studied and studied
and studied.

21
00:01:56.250 --> 00:01:58.490
I've been accepted
to the conservatory.

22
00:01:58.650 --> 00:02:01.210
Among the best grades, in Tehran.

23
00:02:04.410 --> 00:02:06.490
But everything fell apart.

24
00:02:10.050 --> 00:02:13.250
My family and my fiancé's family
have let me down.

25
00:02:13.610 --> 00:02:15.970
My mother told me if I married,

26
00:02:16.130 --> 00:02:18.410
I could do what I liked.

27
00:02:20.170 --> 00:02:21.890
I accepted the deal.

28
00:02:22.850 --> 00:02:24.370
But they betrayed me.

29
00:02:25.810 --> 00:02:27.770
They all betrayed me.

30
00:02:32.730 --> 00:02:34.890
I decided to contact you.

31
00:02:35.050 --> 00:02:37.050
I called you

32
00:02:37.210 --> 00:02:38.930
to beg you to come

33
00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:41.010
and convince them.

34
00:02:42.770 --> 00:02:46.010
My family knows
your films and series.

35
00:02:46.170 --> 00:02:48.530
They watch you every night on TV.

36
00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:51.690
They laugh and cry with you.

37
00:02:56.650 --> 00:02:58.610
They would have listened to you.

38
00:03:01.650 --> 00:03:02.530
I called you.

39
00:03:02.690 --> 00:03:04.650
Many times.

40
00:03:07.850 --> 00:03:09.730
It was useless.

41
00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:13.330
You didn't answer.

42
00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:16.730
You didn't reply to my texts.

43
00:03:21.890 --> 00:03:23.650
I don't see any way out.

44
00:03:29.090 --> 00:03:30.770
Please forgive me.

45
00:03:33.370 --> 00:03:34.410
Forgive me.

46
00:04:19.610 --> 00:04:21.530
Thanks for

47
00:04:22.210 --> 00:04:23.930
listening to me.

48
00:04:52.330 --> 00:04:56.210
I never received anything from her.

49
00:04:57.050 --> 00:04:59.050
Not Instagram nor Telegram.

50
00:04:59.210 --> 00:05:00.730
Nothing at all.

51
00:05:02.530 --> 00:05:06.130
I spent all night searching
this damn phone.

52
00:05:06.290 --> 00:05:09.370
For some trace
that she tried to reach me.

53
00:05:15.330 --> 00:05:18.690
If she's dead,
how could she send this?

54
00:05:19.850 --> 00:05:22.610
She mentions her friend at the start.

55
00:05:22.770 --> 00:05:25.370
They were supposed to meet
in the cave.

56
00:05:26.210 --> 00:05:28.650
She made it before her friend came

57
00:05:29.290 --> 00:05:31.490
and sent it to you.

58
00:05:34.050 --> 00:05:36.730
We'll know more when we arrive.

59
00:05:38.210 --> 00:05:40.210
If she had my number,

60
00:05:40.370 --> 00:05:42.930
why didn't she send it directly?

61
00:05:43.090 --> 00:05:46.650
Where did she get your number?

62
00:05:47.490 --> 00:05:49.490
No idea.

63
00:05:49.650 --> 00:05:53.170
This wouldn't have happened
if you had answered.

64
00:05:53.330 --> 00:05:55.810
She and I speak the same language.

65
00:05:56.250 --> 00:05:59.290
She wanted to use me
to contact you.

66
00:06:00.410 --> 00:06:03.210
She could have contacted you
from the start.

67
00:06:03.410 --> 00:06:05.410
Why drag me into this?

68
00:06:06.490 --> 00:06:08.690
She wanted to be an actress.

69
00:06:08.850 --> 00:06:12.330
She counted on your compassion.

70
00:06:12.650 --> 00:06:15.490
Her family probably recognizes actors

71
00:06:15.650 --> 00:06:17.970
better than filmmakers.

72
00:06:18.730 --> 00:06:21.050
Can I ask you to call Maedeh,

73
00:06:21.210 --> 00:06:24.090
the girl she mentions at the start?

74
00:06:27.570 --> 00:06:29.770
I tried many times.

75
00:06:29.930 --> 00:06:31.970
Her phone is switched off.

76
00:06:38.050 --> 00:06:39.530
See?

77
00:06:46.890 --> 00:06:49.970
What if it's a prank, Mr. Panahi?

78
00:06:51.410 --> 00:06:52.930
Last night,

79
00:06:53.090 --> 00:06:54.890
when I got it,

80
00:06:56.610 --> 00:06:58.250
it was a shock.

81
00:06:58.890 --> 00:07:01.130
I looked for you.

82
00:07:02.130 --> 00:07:04.010
I learned you were shooting.

83
00:07:04.170 --> 00:07:06.490
I called your director.

84
00:07:09.490 --> 00:07:11.970
She called everywhere,

85
00:07:12.130 --> 00:07:14.250
even the Mianeh morgue.

86
00:07:14.450 --> 00:07:16.170
Found nothing.

87
00:07:16.330 --> 00:07:18.730
Why the morgue?

88
00:07:19.010 --> 00:07:21.570
In this kind of case, even in Tehran,

89
00:07:21.730 --> 00:07:25.090
the authorities take over
and keep it quiet.

90
00:07:25.490 --> 00:07:28.330
They classify cases quickly
to avoid attention.

91
00:07:28.530 --> 00:07:30.850
Out in those remote places,

92
00:07:31.010 --> 00:07:33.210
who knows what can happen...

93
00:07:34.330 --> 00:07:37.970
Maybe she called you
on another number.

94
00:07:40.250 --> 00:07:43.970
I do change numbers often
because I get harassed.

95
00:07:44.650 --> 00:07:48.330
I give the old ones to my friends.

96
00:07:49.890 --> 00:07:53.290
Somebody would tell me
about a call like that.

97
00:07:57.210 --> 00:07:59.850
It's strange, it all looks real.

98
00:08:01.370 --> 00:08:04.090
There's no reason to doubt.

99
00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:07.210
But what about that rope and branch?

100
00:08:07.410 --> 00:08:09.450
Did she bring them herself?

101
00:08:10.130 --> 00:08:12.650
When you want to commit suicide,

102
00:08:13.170 --> 00:08:15.650
you find a way.

103
00:08:16.250 --> 00:08:19.210
It's not hard to find
rope and a branch.

104
00:08:19.410 --> 00:08:21.690
She thought of everything.

105
00:08:22.410 --> 00:08:26.370
The branch looks too thin
to support her weight.

106
00:08:27.650 --> 00:08:29.450
Apparently not.

107
00:08:32.050 --> 00:08:35.130
Would you mind
watching the end again?

108
00:08:35.690 --> 00:08:37.730
I get the impression

109
00:08:37.970 --> 00:08:41.610
the shot of her fall at the end
is edited.

110
00:08:43.250 --> 00:08:46.650
Could you stop to look at it closely?

111
00:08:47.730 --> 00:08:49.490
This part, please.

112
00:08:52.570 --> 00:08:55.650
I need to find somewhere
to pull over.

113
00:08:57.330 --> 00:08:58.610
Fine.

114
00:09:31.530 --> 00:09:33.810
It all looks real to me.

115
00:09:36.010 --> 00:09:38.010
When she falls,

116
00:09:38.450 --> 00:09:40.330
I don't see any cut.

117
00:09:40.490 --> 00:09:44.570
Only a real pro
could do such an edit.

118
00:09:45.050 --> 00:09:49.370
There's no way that girl
could do that in her remote village.

119
00:09:50.770 --> 00:09:53.250
It's not the work of an amateur.

120
00:09:56.970 --> 00:09:58.210
'Good evening, Jafar.'

121
00:09:58.410 --> 00:10:00.650
Good evening. How are you?
- 'And you?'

122
00:10:00.810 --> 00:10:02.890
'Is that crazy woman with you?'

123
00:10:03.050 --> 00:10:05.570
'I'm in a real mess.'

124
00:10:05.730 --> 00:10:08.610
'I have one day on this set
with 50 people waiting.'

125
00:10:08.770 --> 00:10:11.770
'She ran out on us
and won't answer her phone.'

126
00:10:11.930 --> 00:10:14.930
'My shoot is stalled.
What should I do?'

127
00:10:15.090 --> 00:10:17.850
I know, but she's very upset.

128
00:10:18.010 --> 00:10:21.730
I didn't want to bring her with me.

129
00:10:21.890 --> 00:10:26.130
She jumped in my car
when she heard I was leaving.

130
00:10:26.330 --> 00:10:27.610
I had no choice.

131
00:10:27.770 --> 00:10:29.810
But in her state,

132
00:10:29.970 --> 00:10:32.770
she's not much use anyway.

133
00:10:32.930 --> 00:10:37.010
'I checked into the case
of that girl.'

134
00:10:37.170 --> 00:10:38.090
I know.

135
00:10:38.250 --> 00:10:40.890
'There's no trace of any of this.'

136
00:10:41.050 --> 00:10:42.890
'She won't accept that.'

137
00:10:43.050 --> 00:10:45.250
'You know what a shoot is like...'

138
00:10:45.450 --> 00:10:48.170
Any news from the morgue?

139
00:10:48.370 --> 00:10:49.970
'Yes, I called them.'

140
00:10:50.130 --> 00:10:53.530
'Nothing matching her description
in the region.'

141
00:10:54.610 --> 00:10:56.170
'I don't know...'

142
00:10:56.370 --> 00:11:00.930
'All of us, we were all very worried.'

143
00:11:01.090 --> 00:11:03.090
'To make matters worse,'

144
00:11:03.250 --> 00:11:07.010
'that nutcase ran off
and left us in this big mess.'

145
00:11:07.170 --> 00:11:10.690
We're approaching the mountains.

146
00:11:10.850 --> 00:11:12.690
We might lose reception.

147
00:11:12.850 --> 00:11:15.210
If I have a signal,

148
00:11:15.410 --> 00:11:18.930
I'll let you know
as soon as we hear something.

149
00:11:19.090 --> 00:11:21.570
I'll call your assistant.

150
00:11:21.730 --> 00:11:23.130
She stepped out.

151
00:11:23.330 --> 00:11:26.570
She's not well.
She's pacing around.

152
00:11:29.370 --> 00:11:31.250
'Try to help me.'

153
00:11:31.450 --> 00:11:32.330
Okay.

154
00:11:33.530 --> 00:11:35.810
'Let me know what's happening.'

155
00:11:35.970 --> 00:11:38.250
I promise.

156
00:11:38.450 --> 00:11:40.370
Nothing else to shoot?

157
00:11:40.530 --> 00:11:43.050
Other shots while waiting?

158
00:11:43.210 --> 00:11:46.090
'I've only got one day here
and she's in it.'

159
00:11:46.250 --> 00:11:48.330
'Put yourself in my shoes.'

160
00:11:49.250 --> 00:11:52.370
'There are no other shots I can do.'

161
00:11:52.530 --> 00:11:57.650
'Running off is one thing.
But she could answer the phone!'

162
00:11:57.810 --> 00:12:01.690
You know, every cloud
has a silver lining.

163
00:12:01.850 --> 00:12:03.970
You'll find a solution.

164
00:12:04.130 --> 00:12:06.930
I hope you'll even gain something
from it.

165
00:12:07.090 --> 00:12:11.090
Sorry, my mother's trying
to reach me.

166
00:12:11.250 --> 00:12:14.210
I need to call to reassure her.

167
00:12:14.410 --> 00:12:17.210
I'm sorry, she's worried too.

168
00:12:17.410 --> 00:12:20.970
Say hi to the crew for me. See you.

169
00:12:25.050 --> 00:12:26.610
Hello, Ma.

170
00:12:27.450 --> 00:12:31.010
Good evening.
I was talking when you called.

171
00:12:31.170 --> 00:12:32.690
How are you?

172
00:12:32.850 --> 00:12:35.690
'Where are you off to?'

173
00:12:35.850 --> 00:12:39.930
Me? Nowhere. Why?

174
00:12:40.090 --> 00:12:41.890
'I'm worried about you.'

175
00:12:42.050 --> 00:12:45.250
'You should tell your mother
when you're leaving.'

176
00:12:45.450 --> 00:12:47.810
'You could come to see me.'

177
00:12:48.450 --> 00:12:53.050
I can't.
I'm travelling with a friend.

178
00:12:53.970 --> 00:12:55.690
'With a friend?'

179
00:12:55.850 --> 00:12:58.570
'I heard you're off making a film.'

180
00:12:59.050 --> 00:13:01.890
No, Ma. That's not true.

181
00:13:02.050 --> 00:13:03.850
Only rumors.

182
00:13:04.010 --> 00:13:07.810
'You're telling me fibs
as well now?'

183
00:13:07.970 --> 00:13:11.010
What fibs are you talking about?

184
00:13:11.170 --> 00:13:14.570
'You could at least tell your mother
what you're up to.'

185
00:13:14.730 --> 00:13:17.050
'Am I your mother or not?'

186
00:13:18.450 --> 00:13:22.210
'I call your home
and they just tell me stories.'

187
00:13:22.650 --> 00:13:25.410
You shouldn't worry so much.

188
00:13:25.570 --> 00:13:28.450
'I need you to let me know
what's happening.'

189
00:13:28.770 --> 00:13:31.010
'Come visit me.'

190
00:13:31.170 --> 00:13:32.610
'I'm all alone.'

191
00:13:32.770 --> 00:13:36.810
You know I visit you very often, Ma.

192
00:13:36.970 --> 00:13:40.370
I had to take a trip.
I'm not making a film.

193
00:13:40.530 --> 00:13:42.570
Rest assured.

194
00:13:43.010 --> 00:13:44.850
If ever I make one,

195
00:13:45.010 --> 00:13:47.810
you'll be the first to know,
I promise.

196
00:13:49.090 --> 00:13:52.050
'You have to let me know
what you're up to.'

197
00:13:52.210 --> 00:13:54.570
'I feel bad when you don't visit.'

198
00:13:54.730 --> 00:13:57.050
'I wonder what you're doing.'

199
00:13:57.210 --> 00:14:01.770
Listen, Ma, I really have to go.

200
00:14:01.930 --> 00:14:03.770
You'll be alright?

201
00:14:03.930 --> 00:14:06.530
'You want to hang up?
Fine, goodbye.'

202
00:14:06.690 --> 00:14:08.970
Love you, bye.

203
00:14:09.130 --> 00:14:10.210
Bye.

204
00:14:24.130 --> 00:14:26.970
Can I see your phone?

205
00:14:34.050 --> 00:14:35.170
Thanks.

206
00:14:43.010 --> 00:14:45.970
'I called you. Several times.'

207
00:14:50.490 --> 00:14:53.410
'Thanks for listening
to this message.'

208
00:16:00.330 --> 00:16:02.210
Did I sleep much?

209
00:16:03.130 --> 00:16:05.690
Good morning. A fair bit, yes.

210
00:16:17.970 --> 00:16:20.010
Can you release the hood?

211
00:16:20.930 --> 00:16:22.650
It's the last button.

212
00:16:23.850 --> 00:16:25.130
Thanks.

213
00:16:43.690 --> 00:16:45.690
Is it still far?

214
00:16:46.610 --> 00:16:48.810
Behind this mountain, I think.

215
00:17:47.930 --> 00:17:51.330
I suggest we start
with the village cemetery.

216
00:17:54.570 --> 00:17:57.770
If she's dead,
we can find a family member.

217
00:18:01.130 --> 00:18:04.010
Or if she's buried,

218
00:18:04.490 --> 00:18:06.090
there will be a new grave.

219
00:18:06.290 --> 00:18:08.970
Why go to the cemetery?

220
00:18:09.050 --> 00:18:10.970
We'll ask people.

221
00:18:11.130 --> 00:18:13.410
But if she lied

222
00:18:14.010 --> 00:18:18.090
or the family hushed it up
to save their honor,

223
00:18:18.490 --> 00:18:20.370
we'll have a hard job.

224
00:18:20.530 --> 00:18:23.370
They can hide everything,

225
00:18:23.850 --> 00:18:25.770
except the body.

226
00:18:26.930 --> 00:18:28.850
No matter how hard they try,

227
00:18:29.010 --> 00:18:30.530
it will come out.

228
00:18:31.210 --> 00:18:33.770
I prefer to check
if she's in the cemetery.

229
00:18:34.690 --> 00:18:38.090
If she's not,
I'll deal with that little bitch.

230
00:18:39.290 --> 00:18:40.970
Maybe with you as well...

231
00:18:42.610 --> 00:18:43.970
Me?

232
00:18:48.410 --> 00:18:52.570
Not long ago,
you came to my place with Tahereh.

233
00:18:53.010 --> 00:18:57.130
You said you were preparing
a screenplay about suicide...

234
00:18:58.050 --> 00:19:00.850
- And?
- With a role for me.

235
00:19:01.370 --> 00:19:02.570
So?

236
00:19:05.130 --> 00:19:06.130
Nothing.

237
00:19:09.770 --> 00:19:10.930
Nothing.

238
00:20:04.450 --> 00:20:06.770
Good morning.
- How can I help?

239
00:20:06.930 --> 00:20:09.810
Which way is Saran village?

240
00:20:10.970 --> 00:20:13.890
I don't speak Persian.
Say it in Turkish.

241
00:20:14.050 --> 00:20:17.290
Sorry, I don't speak Turkish well.

242
00:20:17.450 --> 00:20:20.010
Yes, you do.

243
00:20:20.210 --> 00:20:23.530
You don't forget your mother tongue.

244
00:20:23.690 --> 00:20:26.050
Okay, I'll try.

245
00:20:26.210 --> 00:20:29.370
Tell me,
did something happen here recently?

246
00:20:29.530 --> 00:20:30.850
Shhh!

247
00:20:31.690 --> 00:20:32.890
- Why?
- Horn!

248
00:20:33.050 --> 00:20:34.930
- Sorry?
- Blow your horn.

249
00:20:35.130 --> 00:20:36.410
Blow the horn?

250
00:20:40.610 --> 00:20:42.010
Now twice.

251
00:20:42.210 --> 00:20:43.450
Twice?

252
00:20:45.050 --> 00:20:46.490
Blow it twice?

253
00:20:50.010 --> 00:20:51.970
Longer.

254
00:20:52.170 --> 00:20:54.650
What?
- Blow it longer.

255
00:20:55.010 --> 00:20:56.290
Why?

256
00:21:03.530 --> 00:21:04.450
You can go.

257
00:21:04.610 --> 00:21:05.730
Where?

258
00:21:06.170 --> 00:21:07.290
Which way..

259
00:21:08.130 --> 00:21:09.650
for the village?

260
00:21:09.970 --> 00:21:11.890
Drive to the top of the hill,

261
00:21:12.050 --> 00:21:15.130
go down the other side,

262
00:21:15.290 --> 00:21:17.730
right to the bottom.

263
00:21:17.890 --> 00:21:20.970
Then turn right and you're there.

264
00:21:21.770 --> 00:21:24.210
Thanks a lot, bye.

265
00:21:31.810 --> 00:21:33.530
Did you ask him?

266
00:21:34.970 --> 00:21:36.490
Yes, but...

267
00:22:55.770 --> 00:22:57.090
You see?

268
00:22:57.210 --> 00:22:58.530
What?

269
00:22:59.410 --> 00:23:01.570
That's a wedding.

270
00:23:01.810 --> 00:23:03.730
They're allowed to marry.

271
00:23:03.890 --> 00:23:06.450
Not if there had been a death.

272
00:23:09.170 --> 00:23:11.330
Maybe they are from another village.

273
00:23:11.490 --> 00:23:13.490
Here, every valley

274
00:23:14.330 --> 00:23:16.010
has many villages.

275
00:23:16.890 --> 00:23:19.450
In my opinion, in this kind of place,

276
00:23:19.930 --> 00:23:21.650
if there's mourning,

277
00:23:21.810 --> 00:23:24.290
it's respected all around.

278
00:23:27.650 --> 00:23:28.930
Easy.

279
00:23:29.130 --> 00:23:31.570
You're driving
on the edge of the ravine.

280
00:24:09.610 --> 00:24:12.690
Stop. Something's going on there.

281
00:24:38.890 --> 00:24:39.970
Hello.

282
00:24:40.170 --> 00:24:41.730
Welcome.

283
00:24:41.890 --> 00:24:43.930
Thank you.

284
00:24:44.130 --> 00:24:45.610
Join us for tea.

285
00:24:45.770 --> 00:24:47.770
Thanks, but we should go.

286
00:24:47.930 --> 00:24:52.210
You don't speak Turkish too well.
You can talk to me in Persian.

287
00:24:52.370 --> 00:24:55.170
Thank you. We really should go.

288
00:24:55.330 --> 00:24:58.370
We all must go one day or another.

289
00:24:58.530 --> 00:25:00.530
But take time for tea.

290
00:25:00.690 --> 00:25:01.930
That's kind, thanks.

291
00:25:02.130 --> 00:25:05.970
I've seen this lady before.
I don't know where.

292
00:25:06.170 --> 00:25:09.090
But I don't recognize the gentleman.

293
00:25:09.210 --> 00:25:12.090
Is there another village
farther from here?

294
00:25:12.210 --> 00:25:15.450
Of course.
All over these mountains and valleys,

295
00:25:15.610 --> 00:25:18.090
there are so many villages.

296
00:25:18.210 --> 00:25:21.330
Tell me which one
and I'll guide you.

297
00:25:21.490 --> 00:25:25.050
We're touring,
photographing the landscape.

298
00:25:25.210 --> 00:25:27.090
Everything okay with you?

299
00:25:27.210 --> 00:25:29.490
Of course, everything is fine.

300
00:25:29.650 --> 00:25:31.770
"This world is unjust."

301
00:25:31.930 --> 00:25:35.330
"It knew Noah as well as Solomon."

302
00:25:35.490 --> 00:25:37.690
"It gives children as it takes them."

303
00:25:37.850 --> 00:25:39.490
"All is pain in this world."

304
00:25:39.650 --> 00:25:40.930
But all is well.

305
00:25:41.130 --> 00:25:44.050
Me and you are the problem.

306
00:25:44.210 --> 00:25:46.290
Where is the cemetery?

307
00:25:46.450 --> 00:25:49.170
Are you treasure hunters?

308
00:25:49.330 --> 00:25:50.890
Do we look like we are?

309
00:25:51.090 --> 00:25:54.050
You don't look like
cemetery regulars.

310
00:25:54.210 --> 00:25:55.330
Where is it?

311
00:25:55.490 --> 00:25:58.610
You passed it coming down the hill.

312
00:25:58.770 --> 00:26:00.130
Make a U-turn.

313
00:26:00.290 --> 00:26:02.850
Turn left at the next crossroads.

314
00:26:03.050 --> 00:26:05.330
The cemetery is a bit further on.

315
00:26:05.490 --> 00:26:09.530
Otherwise, there's another one

316
00:26:09.690 --> 00:26:11.330
behind the hill.

317
00:26:11.490 --> 00:26:13.450
It's the old cemetery.

318
00:26:13.610 --> 00:26:15.130
But the treasure is gone.

319
00:26:15.290 --> 00:26:17.450
Thanks. We'll turn back then.

320
00:26:17.610 --> 00:26:20.530
Take care. Bye.

321
00:26:49.090 --> 00:26:50.330
Goodbye.

322
00:26:54.610 --> 00:26:57.210
Why didn't you ask him anything?

323
00:26:59.130 --> 00:27:03.170
We would have talked for hours
without learning a thing.

324
00:27:04.450 --> 00:27:07.130
Something was going on there,

325
00:27:07.650 --> 00:27:09.530
but it didn't smell of death.

326
00:28:15.490 --> 00:28:16.610
Madam...

327
00:28:17.130 --> 00:28:19.450
Why are you lying here?

328
00:28:19.850 --> 00:28:22.850
Hello.
Welcome to my final abode.

329
00:28:23.210 --> 00:28:25.730
My resting place.

330
00:28:26.090 --> 00:28:28.330
God save you.

331
00:28:28.490 --> 00:28:29.970
What did she say?

332
00:28:30.330 --> 00:28:31.770
It's her final abode.

333
00:28:31.970 --> 00:28:33.170
I'm having a hard time.

334
00:28:33.330 --> 00:28:35.410
She had it dug.

335
00:28:36.170 --> 00:28:38.210
I brought a lamp with me.

336
00:28:38.410 --> 00:28:41.410
I put the lamp there,

337
00:28:41.570 --> 00:28:43.370
to have light,

338
00:28:43.650 --> 00:28:47.210
so the grave is lit
for a few hours each night.

339
00:28:47.410 --> 00:28:52.490
Otherwise the snakes will come
to make me pay for the bad I've done.

340
00:28:53.090 --> 00:28:55.610
If there's a light,

341
00:28:55.650 --> 00:28:57.010
it frightens them off.

342
00:28:57.970 --> 00:29:00.450
I'll be rid of them.

343
00:29:02.970 --> 00:29:06.690
You fear snakes?
You don't seem bad.

344
00:29:07.410 --> 00:29:10.010
I'm not necessarily good either.

345
00:29:10.170 --> 00:29:12.810
What good did I do?

346
00:29:13.450 --> 00:29:15.130
Only God knows.

347
00:29:15.290 --> 00:29:16.730
Long life to you.

348
00:29:16.890 --> 00:29:18.650
I hope all goes well.

349
00:29:18.810 --> 00:29:20.210
Take care.

350
00:29:20.410 --> 00:29:21.770
Goodbye.

351
00:29:25.210 --> 00:29:28.410
It's all a set-up.

352
00:29:29.050 --> 00:29:31.490
That girl is playing with us.

353
00:29:31.770 --> 00:29:33.170
Not a sign of her!

354
00:29:33.330 --> 00:29:36.730
It looks like
nobody's been buried here for years.

355
00:29:38.090 --> 00:29:39.690
I'm going mad.

356
00:29:39.850 --> 00:29:42.890
What's all this circus
since last night?

357
00:29:43.090 --> 00:29:44.530
You told me

358
00:29:44.690 --> 00:29:47.370
that the video was made
by a professional.

359
00:29:49.570 --> 00:29:52.570
You asked if there was a cut
at the fall.

360
00:29:52.730 --> 00:29:53.770
Yes.

361
00:29:53.970 --> 00:29:55.850
I looked.

362
00:29:56.050 --> 00:29:59.530
It all looked real.
I didn't see any cut.

363
00:30:00.210 --> 00:30:02.450
I said that if there was a cut,

364
00:30:02.610 --> 00:30:05.770
it wouldn't be the work
of an amateur.

365
00:30:06.210 --> 00:30:08.170
Only a pro could have done it.

366
00:30:08.330 --> 00:30:11.410
There's no such person here,
in the middle of nowhere.

367
00:30:11.570 --> 00:30:12.770
It's all real!

368
00:30:12.970 --> 00:30:15.770
Fine. Will you swear to that?

369
00:30:17.890 --> 00:30:18.890
Swear what?

370
00:30:19.090 --> 00:30:20.970
I'm confused.

371
00:30:21.130 --> 00:30:24.090
I want to be reassured
about you at least.

372
00:30:24.210 --> 00:30:26.890
You want reassurance?

373
00:30:27.450 --> 00:30:30.330
Here's the key. There's the car.

374
00:30:30.490 --> 00:30:33.770
I'll look for a place
to officially take an oath.

375
00:30:34.210 --> 00:30:36.450
Mr. Panahi, I was just playing.

376
00:30:37.130 --> 00:30:39.210
I didn't mean any harm!

377
00:30:40.130 --> 00:30:42.330
Please forgive me.

378
00:30:43.130 --> 00:30:46.450
I regret what I said. Forgive me.

379
00:30:47.370 --> 00:30:50.970
Come on,
I didn't say anything so bad.

380
00:30:51.890 --> 00:30:54.050
Please, Mr. Panahi.

381
00:30:57.690 --> 00:31:01.170
Make an effort,
for the love of your daughter Solmaz.

382
00:32:38.690 --> 00:32:39.610
Careful.

383
00:32:39.930 --> 00:32:42.050
Make room, kids.

384
00:32:42.210 --> 00:32:44.050
Hello.

385
00:32:45.490 --> 00:32:47.210
Don't bother her.

386
00:32:47.370 --> 00:32:49.330
Come on, get out, Madam Jafari.

387
00:32:49.490 --> 00:32:50.930
I don't speak Turkish.

388
00:32:51.090 --> 00:32:52.690
Welcome.

389
00:32:52.890 --> 00:32:55.370
A round of applause for Madam Jafari.

390
00:32:58.450 --> 00:32:59.570
Darn.

391
00:32:59.730 --> 00:33:03.290
- Don't annoy her, kids.
- Thank you.

392
00:33:08.490 --> 00:33:10.010
How are you?

393
00:33:12.730 --> 00:33:15.210
Hello. How are you?

394
00:33:18.410 --> 00:33:21.130
What would you like me to write?

395
00:33:27.770 --> 00:33:30.490
Hold on. What's your name?

396
00:33:32.610 --> 00:33:34.090
Hold on...

397
00:33:35.650 --> 00:33:38.490
"Fereshteh. Good luck."

398
00:33:38.650 --> 00:33:40.610
I'm sorry...

399
00:33:43.050 --> 00:33:45.210
Please sign.

400
00:33:54.010 --> 00:33:56.890
"Good luck."

401
00:34:02.370 --> 00:34:03.450
Hello.

402
00:34:05.770 --> 00:34:07.610
Hello.

403
00:34:17.530 --> 00:34:20.850
Sir, we have too many
water and electricity cuts here.

404
00:34:21.010 --> 00:34:22.690
Not to mention the gas.

405
00:34:22.890 --> 00:34:25.970
Sorry,
we have nothing to do with that.

406
00:34:26.130 --> 00:34:28.650
We thought you came to help us.

407
00:34:28.850 --> 00:34:30.290
I'm very sorry.

408
00:34:30.450 --> 00:34:32.930
Didn't we see you on TV?

409
00:34:33.090 --> 00:34:35.850
You were cooking for your guest?

410
00:34:36.010 --> 00:34:38.290
I can't remember what dish it was.

411
00:34:39.290 --> 00:34:41.370
We could ask them.

412
00:34:41.530 --> 00:34:44.050
Do you know a Marziyeh?

413
00:34:44.730 --> 00:34:47.410
Marziyeh... You know her?

414
00:34:50.690 --> 00:34:51.730
She's my sister.

415
00:34:51.930 --> 00:34:54.410
She's sick.

416
00:34:54.570 --> 00:34:56.170
No, not her.

417
00:34:56.330 --> 00:35:00.290
She says she has a sick sister
named Marziyeh.

418
00:35:00.450 --> 00:35:03.330
That's not who we're looking for.

419
00:35:03.490 --> 00:35:06.050
The girl we're looking for

420
00:35:06.210 --> 00:35:08.490
was accepted into the conservatory.

421
00:35:08.650 --> 00:35:13.530
Oh, so you came here for her,
not for us!

422
00:35:13.850 --> 00:35:16.210
For an empty-headed brat!

423
00:35:16.370 --> 00:35:19.330
We hoped
you could solve our problems.

424
00:35:19.490 --> 00:35:22.130
Come on, let's go.

425
00:35:22.610 --> 00:35:24.690
Everybody go home.

426
00:35:24.890 --> 00:35:27.610
We're left again in our mess!

427
00:35:33.570 --> 00:35:34.930
What's going on?

428
00:35:35.410 --> 00:35:36.530
Incredible.

429
00:35:44.410 --> 00:35:47.370
Marziyeh isn't liked much
in the village.

430
00:35:47.530 --> 00:35:50.610
Her little sister is going
to take you to her house.

431
00:35:50.770 --> 00:35:53.410
Do you know which Marziyeh
this is about?

432
00:35:53.570 --> 00:35:56.010
Let's go. Give me the key.

433
00:36:38.010 --> 00:36:39.450
Hello.

434
00:36:40.930 --> 00:36:43.010
Please come in.

435
00:36:43.170 --> 00:36:45.210
Is this Marziyeh's house?

436
00:36:45.370 --> 00:36:46.810
Ma, where are you going?

437
00:36:46.970 --> 00:36:48.810
Get out!

438
00:36:48.970 --> 00:36:52.530
You won't set foot in here!
Go away!

439
00:36:52.690 --> 00:36:55.050
Don't embarrass me.
- Go!

440
00:36:55.210 --> 00:36:57.490
Where did they come from?

441
00:36:57.650 --> 00:36:59.810
She's not going away to study.

442
00:36:59.970 --> 00:37:02.210
Like that's all there is to do?

443
00:37:02.370 --> 00:37:04.730
Go away!

444
00:37:05.050 --> 00:37:07.930
First studies and then what?

445
00:37:17.690 --> 00:37:19.250
Welcome.

446
00:37:20.730 --> 00:37:22.170
Go ahead.

447
00:37:26.650 --> 00:37:30.090
She won't study.
- I'm ashamed of you. Stop!

448
00:37:30.530 --> 00:37:32.610
I won't!

449
00:37:34.130 --> 00:37:37.010
Why the hell did they come here?

450
00:37:37.210 --> 00:37:40.850
Studies? What the hell for?

451
00:37:42.450 --> 00:37:43.450
Stupid brat!

452
00:37:43.650 --> 00:37:46.450
Leave me alone!
I won't let her do studies!

453
00:37:46.610 --> 00:37:50.130
She dishonors us!

454
00:38:00.210 --> 00:38:01.770
You bad boy!

455
00:38:04.770 --> 00:38:06.250
Let's go, sweetie.

456
00:38:07.490 --> 00:38:09.890
Please, follow me.

457
00:38:21.290 --> 00:38:23.210
I'm sorry, come in.

458
00:38:23.370 --> 00:38:25.930
Thank you, ma'am.
It's fine here.

459
00:38:26.250 --> 00:38:28.130
Are you sure? Sit down then.

460
00:38:28.290 --> 00:38:30.490
We don't want to be a bother.

461
00:38:30.650 --> 00:38:31.890
Thank you.

462
00:38:36.130 --> 00:38:38.010
What was he saying?

463
00:38:38.170 --> 00:38:40.770
Nothing. A bunch of insults.

464
00:38:44.250 --> 00:38:45.850
Did he mention her?

465
00:38:46.010 --> 00:38:48.610
He wasn't making much sense.

466
00:38:49.090 --> 00:38:50.650
He wasn't clear.

467
00:38:51.810 --> 00:38:54.810
It was gibberish.

468
00:39:04.810 --> 00:39:06.890
There's no sign of...

469
00:39:09.930 --> 00:39:11.810
Don't put yourself out.

470
00:39:13.090 --> 00:39:15.330
Welcome.

471
00:39:16.650 --> 00:39:19.290
I thought you might be coming.

472
00:39:19.450 --> 00:39:21.530
I wish it was another time.

473
00:39:21.730 --> 00:39:24.090
We'll lose face in the village.

474
00:39:24.810 --> 00:39:28.130
Why do you say that?
- It's because...

475
00:39:28.290 --> 00:39:29.930
Marziyeh has been gone

476
00:39:30.090 --> 00:39:31.970
for three days.

477
00:39:33.170 --> 00:39:37.010
We looked for her everywhere.
We haven't found her.

478
00:39:37.290 --> 00:39:39.570
Before, when she got angry,

479
00:39:39.770 --> 00:39:41.650
she went to her aunt's.

480
00:39:41.850 --> 00:39:43.930
She's not there either.

481
00:39:44.610 --> 00:39:46.850
Her father went to Tehran,

482
00:39:47.890 --> 00:39:51.290
in case she went there
to the conservatory.

483
00:39:52.330 --> 00:39:54.570
Her fiancé's family don't know.

484
00:39:54.770 --> 00:39:56.570
I hope he'll be back soon.

485
00:39:57.010 --> 00:39:59.370
Or Mehdi will cause a scandal.

486
00:39:59.970 --> 00:40:02.850
If the fiancé's family find out,

487
00:40:03.330 --> 00:40:05.170
it will be the end for her.

488
00:40:08.450 --> 00:40:11.810
- That's her brother?
- Yes, her younger brother.

489
00:40:13.850 --> 00:40:16.050
Why don't you call her?

490
00:40:16.210 --> 00:40:18.970
We did. Her phone is switched off.

491
00:40:19.410 --> 00:40:23.130
Ask her friends.
- She doesn't have any.

492
00:40:23.490 --> 00:40:27.370
The villagers don't let their girls
socialize with Marziyeh.

493
00:40:27.530 --> 00:40:30.610
For fear they'll become
as empty-headed as her.

494
00:40:30.970 --> 00:40:33.490
"We don't want entertainers here",
they say.

495
00:40:34.050 --> 00:40:35.010
Entertainers...

496
00:40:36.570 --> 00:40:38.610
I haven't heard that in a while.

497
00:40:42.010 --> 00:40:43.330
Roghieh.

498
00:40:43.490 --> 00:40:45.650
Will you see who rang?

499
00:40:45.850 --> 00:40:49.090
My daughter was the most gifted,
the most clever.

500
00:40:49.250 --> 00:40:52.370
Her problem is
she doesn't know when to shut up.

501
00:40:52.850 --> 00:40:55.450
She says everything she thinks.

502
00:40:55.610 --> 00:40:57.650
That doesn't please everybody.

503
00:40:57.850 --> 00:41:00.370
Once she got it into her head
to study,

504
00:41:00.530 --> 00:41:02.970
I knew it wouldn't end well.

505
00:41:03.730 --> 00:41:06.570
I thought marriage
would make her forget.

506
00:41:06.770 --> 00:41:09.090
But she imposed her conditions.

507
00:41:09.250 --> 00:41:11.610
We had to accept them.

508
00:41:11.810 --> 00:41:16.050
Her father said the conservatory
is extremely selective,

509
00:41:16.210 --> 00:41:19.770
that she would never be accepted.

510
00:41:20.130 --> 00:41:23.570
I took her to the audition in secret.

511
00:41:23.770 --> 00:41:27.370
My bad luck she was accepted!
I don't know what to do.

512
00:41:29.170 --> 00:41:31.010
Would Maedeh know where she is?

513
00:41:31.170 --> 00:41:33.370
How do you know Maedeh?

514
00:41:33.530 --> 00:41:37.610
A reference is needed to apply
to the conservatory.

515
00:41:37.810 --> 00:41:39.730
Marziyeh put Maedeh's name.

516
00:41:39.890 --> 00:41:42.410
They are cousins.
- Does she live here?

517
00:41:42.570 --> 00:41:45.730
Yes, nearby.
You're badly seated.

518
00:41:45.890 --> 00:41:47.570
No worries.

519
00:41:47.770 --> 00:41:50.010
Can we go and see Maedeh?

520
00:41:50.170 --> 00:41:53.050
No, stay here.
I'll send Rogieh to get her.

521
00:41:53.210 --> 00:41:55.490
Go and get Maedeh.

522
00:41:55.650 --> 00:41:57.810
Let's go in the car.

523
00:41:57.970 --> 00:41:59.770
We'll wait in the car.

524
00:41:59.930 --> 00:42:02.850
Thanks. When she arrives,
she'll come to see us.

525
00:42:03.010 --> 00:42:06.450
Thank you so much, ma'am.

526
00:42:06.610 --> 00:42:08.050
That's very kind.

527
00:42:08.210 --> 00:42:11.130
I'll bring tea.
- No thanks.

528
00:42:11.610 --> 00:42:15.290
Don't put yourself
to all that trouble, ma'am.

529
00:42:16.290 --> 00:42:19.090
You should stay. Maedeh is coming.

530
00:42:19.730 --> 00:42:22.090
We'll wait for her in the car.

531
00:42:22.250 --> 00:42:24.210
Don't mention it to anybody.

532
00:42:24.370 --> 00:42:27.530
Of course.
Thanks a lot. Goodbye.

533
00:42:28.370 --> 00:42:30.210
Don't worry.

534
00:42:33.130 --> 00:42:35.610
Thank you. Goodbye.

535
00:42:37.290 --> 00:42:38.810
No need to see us out.

536
00:42:38.970 --> 00:42:40.930
Goodbye.

537
00:42:53.050 --> 00:42:55.770
Gone for three days...
Think she's dead?

538
00:42:56.410 --> 00:42:57.730
I don't know.

539
00:43:32.250 --> 00:43:34.730
Madam Jafari! I don't believe it!

540
00:43:34.890 --> 00:43:37.690
Go home, dear.
Your mother will be worried.

541
00:43:37.850 --> 00:43:39.730
How are you?

542
00:43:40.530 --> 00:43:43.010
What are you doing here?

543
00:43:43.250 --> 00:43:46.770
Maedeh, tell me where she is.
- Who?

544
00:43:46.930 --> 00:43:50.970
Listen, I'm in no mood for games.

545
00:43:51.130 --> 00:43:54.330
Stop playing games. I've had enough.

546
00:43:54.850 --> 00:43:56.330
I don't understand.

547
00:43:56.490 --> 00:43:59.530
Where is Marziyeh?
- She's not at home?

548
00:43:59.730 --> 00:44:01.170
Come here.

549
00:44:01.330 --> 00:44:04.730
You sent me a video on Telegram,
didn't you?

550
00:44:04.890 --> 00:44:06.810
I don't have a mobile.

551
00:44:08.650 --> 00:44:10.170
Mr. Panahi...

552
00:44:10.330 --> 00:44:12.010
give me your phone.

553
00:44:13.930 --> 00:44:15.210
Unlock it.

554
00:44:18.690 --> 00:44:20.490
Whose number is this?

555
00:44:22.930 --> 00:44:24.890
Marziyeh's.

556
00:44:25.250 --> 00:44:27.970
What's up? I'm getting worried.

557
00:44:28.210 --> 00:44:29.810
I don't understand.

558
00:44:29.970 --> 00:44:31.530
Madam Jafari.

559
00:44:31.930 --> 00:44:34.890
Mr. Panahi, did something happen?

560
00:44:35.050 --> 00:44:36.090
Mr. Panahi...

561
00:44:36.250 --> 00:44:38.930
No, it's nothing.

562
00:44:40.650 --> 00:44:42.730
When did you last see Marziyeh?

563
00:44:42.890 --> 00:44:44.850
A couple of days ago.

564
00:44:45.490 --> 00:44:47.450
She didn't tell you anything?

565
00:44:47.850 --> 00:44:49.530
Like what?

566
00:44:50.490 --> 00:44:53.250
I don't know.
Maybe about her studies.

567
00:44:53.410 --> 00:44:55.730
She talks about them all the time.

568
00:44:55.890 --> 00:44:58.690
She didn't say when she was leaving?

569
00:44:59.010 --> 00:45:01.490
How could she, poor thing?

570
00:45:01.690 --> 00:45:03.770
She's desperate.

571
00:45:04.690 --> 00:45:07.650
Do you know anything, Mr. Panahi?

572
00:45:09.650 --> 00:45:11.530
It seems she knows nothing.

573
00:45:13.730 --> 00:45:15.170
Mr. Panahi...

574
00:45:15.970 --> 00:45:18.330
Is there a cave near here?
- Why?

575
00:45:18.490 --> 00:45:20.170
To know.

576
00:45:20.890 --> 00:45:22.850
Yes, that way.

577
00:45:23.010 --> 00:45:25.290
You will see the mountains.

578
00:45:27.490 --> 00:45:29.050
Mr. Panahi...

579
00:45:29.290 --> 00:45:30.410
Excuse me.

580
00:45:39.370 --> 00:45:43.130
Did something happen to her?
Please tell me.

581
00:45:43.290 --> 00:45:45.450
No, nothing happened.

582
00:45:45.650 --> 00:45:49.810
Just don't say anything
to anybody. Okay?

583
00:45:50.170 --> 00:45:52.450
Say nothing, to nobody.

584
00:45:52.650 --> 00:45:54.770
Promise?
- Yes.

585
00:45:55.170 --> 00:45:58.130
Take care.
- Thanks. Goodbye.

586
00:47:36.930 --> 00:47:38.890
Mr. Panahi, it's here!

587
00:47:55.930 --> 00:47:58.330
There, the branch.

588
00:47:59.090 --> 00:48:00.450
What about the rope?

589
00:48:00.650 --> 00:48:03.930
The body, the phone and all that,
where are they?

590
00:48:05.090 --> 00:48:07.650
I told you it was all staged.

591
00:48:13.010 --> 00:48:15.930
You expect all that to be here?

592
00:48:16.330 --> 00:48:18.570
They took it all probably.
- Who?

593
00:48:18.730 --> 00:48:20.370
Her family.

594
00:48:20.570 --> 00:48:24.290
You know they would hide everything
to save face.

595
00:48:24.450 --> 00:48:29.290
But they said they hadn't heard
from her for three days!

596
00:48:29.610 --> 00:48:32.570
If they are covering up,
they would not tell us.

597
00:48:32.730 --> 00:48:35.450
So they staged this for us?

598
00:48:35.970 --> 00:48:38.010
No, for their honor.

599
00:49:19.410 --> 00:49:20.970
Hello.

600
00:49:25.730 --> 00:49:27.370
Have a seat.

601
00:49:27.570 --> 00:49:30.690
Thanks. Don't get up.

602
00:49:35.210 --> 00:49:37.170
How are you?

603
00:49:37.330 --> 00:49:40.370
What would you like?
- What do you have?

604
00:49:40.730 --> 00:49:42.930
Fresh eggs, they're very good.

605
00:49:43.090 --> 00:49:45.770
Just two teas, thanks.

606
00:49:47.970 --> 00:49:50.090
We're honored by your presence.

607
00:49:50.250 --> 00:49:51.890
Welcome.

608
00:49:52.050 --> 00:49:55.330
Sorry I didn't recognize you
on the road. I learned later.

609
00:49:55.490 --> 00:49:56.850
I'm very sorry.

610
00:49:57.010 --> 00:49:58.930
They are welcoming us.

611
00:49:59.090 --> 00:50:02.090
He's apologizing
for not recognizing you.

612
00:50:02.250 --> 00:50:04.050
No problem.

613
00:50:04.650 --> 00:50:08.050
That business with the horn earlier,
what was it?

614
00:50:08.210 --> 00:50:11.410
I thought you understood.

615
00:50:12.170 --> 00:50:15.810
I did... but tell me more.

616
00:50:16.210 --> 00:50:18.210
Do you mind if I explain?

617
00:50:20.810 --> 00:50:24.210
In fact, in our village,

618
00:50:24.810 --> 00:50:26.730
the only road, that you saw,

619
00:50:26.890 --> 00:50:29.530
is very rough and narrow.

620
00:50:30.730 --> 00:50:34.450
Only one car can pass at a time.
You honk at the bend

621
00:50:34.650 --> 00:50:36.810
to know if the road's clear.

622
00:50:36.970 --> 00:50:39.850
If so, you can go on.

623
00:50:40.010 --> 00:50:42.650
If not, the car on the other side

624
00:50:42.810 --> 00:50:45.770
honks to show it's there.

625
00:50:45.930 --> 00:50:47.330
You know it's coming.

626
00:50:47.530 --> 00:50:51.570
If you don't honk back,
that means the other one can pass.

627
00:50:51.730 --> 00:50:55.170
If he's in a rush, he honks twice.

628
00:50:55.330 --> 00:50:57.090
It's the emergency signal.

629
00:50:57.250 --> 00:51:01.050
What do you do in this case? Wait.

630
00:51:01.210 --> 00:51:03.050
Wait for the other to pass.

631
00:51:03.210 --> 00:51:06.530
If you're in a hurry too,
you honk longer.

632
00:51:06.690 --> 00:51:09.210
To signal a real emergency,

633
00:51:09.370 --> 00:51:11.050
like a sick passenger.

634
00:51:11.210 --> 00:51:12.610
Then, you can pass.

635
00:51:12.770 --> 00:51:15.970
We set this rule together.

636
00:51:16.210 --> 00:51:18.810
You make your own rules.

637
00:51:18.970 --> 00:51:20.690
Of course, sir.

638
00:51:20.850 --> 00:51:23.090
Everything falls apart without rules.

639
00:51:23.250 --> 00:51:25.050
Common sense is necessary.

640
00:51:25.210 --> 00:51:29.010
In this village, for example,

641
00:51:29.170 --> 00:51:31.090
we've got nice gardens,

642
00:51:31.250 --> 00:51:35.570
fine orchards, generous soil.

643
00:51:35.730 --> 00:51:38.330
But if somebody falls ill one day,

644
00:51:38.530 --> 00:51:43.610
are the garden, the orchard
or the soil going to cure him?

645
00:51:43.810 --> 00:51:45.130
Of course not.

646
00:51:45.290 --> 00:51:47.850
We need doctors.

647
00:51:48.010 --> 00:51:51.810
To treat us when we're sick.

648
00:51:52.570 --> 00:51:54.570
In this village,

649
00:51:54.730 --> 00:51:58.010
there are more satellite dishes
than people.

650
00:51:58.250 --> 00:52:03.050
Tomorrow, if they're sick,
who's going to treat them?

651
00:52:03.210 --> 00:52:05.130
Satellite dishes

652
00:52:05.290 --> 00:52:07.930
or wannabe entertainers?

653
00:52:08.090 --> 00:52:10.410
Neither one can cure them.

654
00:52:11.930 --> 00:52:15.330
That girl won't listen to reason.

655
00:52:16.090 --> 00:52:18.610
She does what suits her.

656
00:52:19.210 --> 00:52:21.210
Really empty-headed!

657
00:52:21.370 --> 00:52:25.170
What did you come all this way for?

658
00:52:25.730 --> 00:52:28.650
She won't listen...

659
00:52:28.810 --> 00:52:31.610
And if somebody
wants to be an entertainer,

660
00:52:31.930 --> 00:52:34.210
what should they do?

661
00:52:34.370 --> 00:52:36.370
That won't do at all.

662
00:52:36.570 --> 00:52:38.650
We have a saying in the village:

663
00:52:38.810 --> 00:52:40.730
Let a corpse do what it likes

664
00:52:41.170 --> 00:52:42.930
and it will shit itself.

665
00:52:43.090 --> 00:52:46.410
You know how much trouble we go to

666
00:52:46.610 --> 00:52:48.250
for our animals?

667
00:52:50.650 --> 00:52:55.410
Our lives depend on them.
We have to struggle not to lose them.

668
00:52:56.050 --> 00:52:58.810
Without them, we can't survive.

669
00:52:59.410 --> 00:53:02.330
That young girl
needs to understand something:

670
00:53:02.530 --> 00:53:05.330
if an entertainer's life
was enviable,

671
00:53:05.530 --> 00:53:09.690
then Madam Shahrzad,
who once had her time of glory,

672
00:53:09.850 --> 00:53:14.050
would not find herself
now living all alone,

673
00:53:14.530 --> 00:53:17.690
so miserably in her little house.

674
00:53:17.850 --> 00:53:19.610
Who's Shahrzad?

675
00:53:20.210 --> 00:53:23.410
A lady who danced and sang in films

676
00:53:23.610 --> 00:53:26.610
before the Revolution.

677
00:53:50.690 --> 00:53:52.370
Mr. Panahi!

678
00:53:52.690 --> 00:53:54.250
Not that way, this way.

679
00:53:56.290 --> 00:53:58.170
Hurry up.

680
00:54:02.970 --> 00:54:04.770
See what you've done to me?

681
00:54:04.930 --> 00:54:07.730
I moved Heaven and Earth
since yesterday

682
00:54:07.890 --> 00:54:12.010
to try to find you, you little brat!

683
00:54:12.610 --> 00:54:15.810
And you're playing hide-and-seek?
- Listen!

684
00:54:15.970 --> 00:54:17.810
Have you no shame?
- Forgive me.

685
00:54:17.970 --> 00:54:20.410
What should I forgive?

686
00:54:21.690 --> 00:54:23.410
Are you kidding me?

687
00:54:29.210 --> 00:54:30.810
Listen, Behnaz!

688
00:54:30.970 --> 00:54:33.170
Don't use my first name!

689
00:54:33.370 --> 00:54:35.850
Shut up!

690
00:54:37.330 --> 00:54:39.890
I've had it with you!

691
00:54:40.050 --> 00:54:44.170
I let a child manipulate me!
- Allow me to explain.

692
00:54:44.330 --> 00:54:46.930
No, I won't allow you!

693
00:54:47.090 --> 00:54:49.170
I won't allow you to do anything!

694
00:54:52.130 --> 00:54:53.730
Don't hit her!

695
00:54:54.250 --> 00:54:55.570
Out of my way!

696
00:54:56.930 --> 00:54:58.010
Shut up!

697
00:54:58.170 --> 00:55:00.410
You pretended you had no news!

698
00:55:03.690 --> 00:55:06.010
Why lie, you little bitch?

699
00:55:06.170 --> 00:55:09.530
Why did you lie to me?

700
00:55:09.690 --> 00:55:11.810
Why did I lie to you?

701
00:55:11.970 --> 00:55:13.890
Why lie?

702
00:55:14.490 --> 00:55:18.610
You were the only one
who could save me!

703
00:55:18.770 --> 00:55:20.810
I wouldn't have lied otherwise.

704
00:55:20.970 --> 00:55:22.450
Can't you understand?

705
00:55:23.010 --> 00:55:24.650
Can't you understand?

706
00:55:24.810 --> 00:55:26.850
Please, Madam Jafari.

707
00:55:27.010 --> 00:55:30.450
I beg you.
Try to understand me.

708
00:55:30.930 --> 00:55:32.570
Please.

709
00:55:32.730 --> 00:55:34.650
I had no choice.

710
00:55:34.810 --> 00:55:37.730
You were my only hope
to attend the conservatory.

711
00:55:37.890 --> 00:55:39.530
You empty-headed girl...

712
00:55:39.690 --> 00:55:41.930
You call me empty-headed as well!

713
00:55:42.090 --> 00:55:44.330
You talk like the others!

714
00:55:45.610 --> 00:55:48.650
I beg you.
Try to understand.

715
00:55:49.210 --> 00:55:52.010
You're the only one who can help me.

716
00:55:52.890 --> 00:55:55.970
I tried everything. Everything!

717
00:55:56.250 --> 00:55:58.610
I saw no other solution.

718
00:55:58.770 --> 00:56:00.970
And I owe you something as well?

719
00:56:01.210 --> 00:56:03.010
What do I owe you?

720
00:56:03.490 --> 00:56:05.570
Couldn't you have simply asked me?

721
00:56:05.730 --> 00:56:09.650
If I had asked you,
if I had told the truth,

722
00:56:09.810 --> 00:56:11.570
would you have come?

723
00:56:11.730 --> 00:56:13.690
Would you really have come?

724
00:56:14.650 --> 00:56:16.930
Please, Madam Jafari.

725
00:56:17.170 --> 00:56:19.930
I beg you.

726
00:56:20.090 --> 00:56:23.170
I'll get down on my knees
if it helps.

727
00:56:23.330 --> 00:56:26.290
Don't go!
This time my brother will kill me

728
00:56:26.490 --> 00:56:28.610
for disappearing for three days.

729
00:56:28.770 --> 00:56:31.130
He'll set fire to Shahrzad's house.

730
00:56:31.290 --> 00:56:34.730
He'll destroy everything
if he learns I was at her place.

731
00:56:35.010 --> 00:56:36.570
I beg you.

732
00:56:40.730 --> 00:56:42.650
Please, don't leave!

733
00:56:44.130 --> 00:56:46.170
Why can't they understand?

734
00:57:19.610 --> 00:57:21.970
Hello, how are you?
- Fine thanks.

735
00:57:22.130 --> 00:57:24.970
Have you got a mobile?
Is there a signal?

736
00:57:25.130 --> 00:57:26.570
Wait, I'll check.

737
00:57:29.090 --> 00:57:31.730
No, no signal. What's going on?

738
00:57:31.890 --> 00:57:34.570
We were leading the bull and he fell.

739
00:57:34.730 --> 00:57:36.210
What will you do?

740
00:57:36.410 --> 00:57:38.130
What can I do?

741
00:57:38.290 --> 00:57:40.130
Not a whole lot.

742
00:57:40.290 --> 00:57:44.010
My colleague went up the hill
to try for a signal.

743
00:57:44.170 --> 00:57:48.330
He'll try to reach a veterinarian,
if there's reception.

744
00:57:49.450 --> 00:57:54.850
If not, he'll go to the village
to call from a landline.

745
00:57:55.450 --> 00:57:57.810
The poor animal will be dead by then.

746
00:57:57.970 --> 00:58:01.730
What else can I do? Tell me.

747
00:58:01.890 --> 00:58:05.730
I can help you to push it to the side
so we can drive past.

748
00:58:05.890 --> 00:58:07.490
That's what you think.

749
00:58:07.650 --> 00:58:10.130
He's all swollen, look at his belly.

750
00:58:10.290 --> 00:58:13.170
If we touch him, he'll die.

751
00:58:13.490 --> 00:58:17.210
We can't just wait here.
You could put it out of its misery.

752
00:58:17.410 --> 00:58:19.930
God forbid!

753
00:58:20.090 --> 00:58:21.410
I did honk though.

754
00:58:21.570 --> 00:58:25.970
You could have responded
so that I wouldn't advance.

755
00:58:26.290 --> 00:58:31.290
I heard you but I thought
it was my colleague with the vet.

756
00:58:31.730 --> 00:58:34.650
A vet in the village? Fat chance!

757
00:58:34.930 --> 00:58:37.490
I think you'd be better

758
00:58:37.650 --> 00:58:40.210
cutting your losses.

759
00:58:40.730 --> 00:58:45.730
Even humans are put
out of their misery.

760
00:58:45.890 --> 00:58:47.090
Do it for him.

761
00:58:47.250 --> 00:58:50.530
It's a sin.
And I've only got a small knife.

762
00:58:50.690 --> 00:58:54.010
I couldn't,
I don't want him to suffer.

763
00:58:54.170 --> 00:58:55.530
He's already suffering.

764
00:58:55.690 --> 00:58:58.050
Yes, but that's different.

765
00:58:58.210 --> 00:59:02.210
He's suffering but it's not up
to you or me to intervene.

766
00:59:02.410 --> 00:59:04.650
It's God's will.

767
00:59:05.050 --> 00:59:07.650
If I put the knife to him,

768
00:59:07.810 --> 00:59:10.010
we'll both be responsible.

769
00:59:10.170 --> 00:59:12.090
That's not just any bull.

770
00:59:12.250 --> 00:59:15.050
He's the bull with the golden balls.

771
00:59:15.210 --> 00:59:16.970
What?
- He's a stud.

772
00:59:17.130 --> 00:59:19.290
Know what I mean?
- No.

773
00:59:19.570 --> 00:59:22.450
Does the lady speak Turkish?

774
00:59:22.610 --> 00:59:23.890
No, she doesn't.

775
00:59:24.050 --> 00:59:25.610
Then I'll explain.

776
00:59:25.770 --> 00:59:28.450
He's a stud bull.

777
00:59:28.610 --> 00:59:32.210
He's not a regular bull.
He's very special.

778
00:59:33.170 --> 00:59:35.850
He's used for breeding.

779
00:59:36.010 --> 00:59:39.130
You only see a fallen bull
blocking your car.

780
00:59:39.290 --> 00:59:41.770
But nowhere in Azerbaijan,

781
00:59:41.930 --> 00:59:44.890
nor all of Iran,
will you find a bull like him.

782
00:59:45.050 --> 00:59:48.690
He's of a breed apart,
with special genes,

783
00:59:48.850 --> 00:59:50.690
a unique specimen.

784
00:59:51.050 --> 00:59:53.610
I've seen with my own eyes.

785
00:59:53.930 --> 00:59:57.930
In one night, he impregnated 10 cows!

786
00:59:58.370 --> 01:00:02.010
I get 300,000 tomans per breeding.

787
01:00:02.970 --> 01:00:05.250
Tomorrow, there's a big fair here.

788
01:00:05.450 --> 01:00:07.250
People come from all over,

789
01:00:07.450 --> 01:00:09.890
with trucks full of heifers.

790
01:00:10.050 --> 01:00:12.690
You can imagine the scene.

791
01:00:12.850 --> 01:00:16.170
I can already see the trucks
lining up for him.

792
01:00:16.370 --> 01:00:18.050
Local cows are the worst.

793
01:00:18.210 --> 01:00:22.170
One sniff of him
and they moo with desire.

794
01:00:22.370 --> 01:00:25.930
Spend the night here
and you'll hear for yourself.

795
01:00:26.570 --> 01:00:30.210
It's like a symphonic orchestra
when they all get going!

796
01:00:30.410 --> 01:00:32.010
He's one-of-a-kind.

797
01:00:32.170 --> 01:00:34.330
And he had to fall...

798
01:00:34.490 --> 01:00:38.850
When the heifers arrive tomorrow,
what will I tell them?

799
01:00:39.010 --> 01:00:43.370
He cannot be replaced
if something happens to him.

800
01:00:43.530 --> 01:00:46.010
- Know why?
- Why?

801
01:00:46.170 --> 01:00:48.450
His testicles are miraculous.

802
01:00:48.610 --> 01:00:52.330
Give a kebab of them
to an old man of 80,

803
01:00:52.490 --> 01:00:53.650
he'll become a beast!

804
01:00:53.810 --> 01:00:55.610
Let's go back, Mr. Panahi.

805
01:00:55.770 --> 01:00:58.330
We have to go, goodbye.

806
01:00:58.490 --> 01:01:01.730
I'll leave you my card.
You never know.

807
01:01:01.890 --> 01:01:04.130
If you need a pick-me-up,

808
01:01:04.330 --> 01:01:07.050
we do express deliveries of kebabs.

809
01:01:07.210 --> 01:01:09.770
Thank you. Goodbye.

810
01:01:32.890 --> 01:01:35.890
Listen, think what you want,

811
01:01:36.050 --> 01:01:39.730
but I find you were very hard on her.

812
01:01:39.890 --> 01:01:42.690
People here aren't used to that.

813
01:01:42.970 --> 01:01:45.130
They're offended quickly,

814
01:01:45.730 --> 01:01:47.810
but forget even more quickly.

815
01:01:48.810 --> 01:01:50.730
Since we're going back,

816
01:01:51.090 --> 01:01:53.570
try to make up with her.

817
01:01:54.410 --> 01:01:56.210
But it's up to you.

818
01:01:57.330 --> 01:01:58.130
Hello.

819
01:01:58.330 --> 01:02:00.770
How are you?
- Fine, thanks.

820
01:02:04.050 --> 01:02:06.850
I was told Shahrzad
lives around here.

821
01:02:07.010 --> 01:02:08.850
A bit further, on the left.

822
01:02:09.010 --> 01:02:10.410
Thanks.

823
01:02:29.570 --> 01:02:30.890
Hello.

824
01:02:32.130 --> 01:02:33.610
Thanks for coming back.

825
01:02:41.610 --> 01:02:43.010
Mr. Panahi...

826
01:02:43.170 --> 01:02:44.930
Wait, please.

827
01:02:45.090 --> 01:02:46.530
One minute.

828
01:02:52.810 --> 01:02:54.330
Excuse me, Mr. Panahi.

829
01:02:54.490 --> 01:02:56.530
Something's up. I'll go check.

830
01:02:56.690 --> 01:02:58.850
What?
- I'll let you know.

831
01:02:59.010 --> 01:03:01.890
Wait for me here.
Need anything?

832
01:07:06.970 --> 01:07:10.210
Good you didn't come.
The place is tiny.

833
01:07:10.410 --> 01:07:12.210
Embarrassing for her.

834
01:07:12.410 --> 01:07:14.210
What happened?

835
01:07:14.370 --> 01:07:17.450
Nothing.
She's angry at the whole world.

836
01:07:18.650 --> 01:07:21.050
Especially directors she worked with.

837
01:07:22.130 --> 01:07:24.970
She says they hurt her a lot.

838
01:07:26.570 --> 01:07:30.090
I told her you weren't making films
at that time.

839
01:07:30.290 --> 01:07:32.290
She replied: "All alike!"

840
01:07:32.450 --> 01:07:35.490
"One worse than the other!"

841
01:07:36.210 --> 01:07:38.090
She must resent us

842
01:07:38.290 --> 01:07:40.570
for not supporting her.

843
01:07:40.730 --> 01:07:42.490
But she wasn't alone.

844
01:07:42.650 --> 01:07:45.930
All those actors back then
faced the same problem.

845
01:07:48.610 --> 01:07:52.090
She's got nothing in her house.
Just her paintings

846
01:07:52.330 --> 01:07:54.210
and posters of her films.

847
01:07:54.370 --> 01:07:55.770
That's how it is.

848
01:07:58.370 --> 01:08:00.530
I proposed to Marziyeh

849
01:08:00.690 --> 01:08:02.770
to take her home before leaving.

850
01:08:02.930 --> 01:08:06.290
She wants to wait her father's return
from Tehran tomorrow.

851
01:08:06.450 --> 01:08:09.090
He seems less narrow-minded
than the brother.

852
01:08:09.290 --> 01:08:11.650
But it's as you like.

853
01:08:11.810 --> 01:08:13.930
Do we have a choice?

854
01:08:14.410 --> 01:08:17.490
Not really.
But what are you going to do?

855
01:08:18.890 --> 01:08:20.450
Nothing.

856
01:08:22.770 --> 01:08:24.570
I'm fine. I'll stay here.

857
01:08:24.730 --> 01:08:26.090
No.

858
01:08:26.290 --> 01:08:30.450
If the villagers find out,
they won't accept this.

859
01:08:30.610 --> 01:08:33.090
I want to stay here.

860
01:08:33.290 --> 01:08:34.850
I'll sleep in the car.

861
01:08:35.010 --> 01:08:36.850
I'm tired.

862
01:08:38.290 --> 01:08:42.090
I'm safer here than anywhere else.

863
01:08:42.650 --> 01:08:46.330
I'll leave you this.
They're from here, they're delicious.

864
01:08:46.730 --> 01:08:49.690
There's tea as well.
I'll bring you some.

865
01:08:49.850 --> 01:08:52.690
She also gave me a CD of her poetry.

866
01:08:52.850 --> 01:08:53.850
She recites?

867
01:08:54.010 --> 01:08:56.170
Yes, she recorded it in Kerman.

868
01:08:56.330 --> 01:09:00.210
They just arrived, she gave me one.
I'll leave it with you.

869
01:09:00.410 --> 01:09:01.610
Thank you.

870
01:09:01.770 --> 01:09:03.290
You don't need anything?

871
01:09:03.450 --> 01:09:04.650
Good evening.

872
01:09:53.130 --> 01:09:56.370
'I had reached
the summit of uncertainty'

873
01:09:56.610 --> 01:09:59.730
'Desiring to know the names'

874
01:10:00.370 --> 01:10:02.050
'The head mistress' hand'

875
01:10:02.210 --> 01:10:05.490
'made the hammer dance in the air'

876
01:10:06.290 --> 01:10:10.810
'Breaking the silence
of the immaculate dawn'

877
01:10:11.970 --> 01:10:14.690
'Banging against the red metal object'

878
01:10:14.850 --> 01:10:19.010
'pinned on the schoolyard pine tree'

879
01:10:20.210 --> 01:10:23.650
'Ring, Ring, Ring'

880
01:10:24.290 --> 01:10:28.210
'The silence tortured the innocence'

881
01:10:28.650 --> 01:10:30.170
'The first prayer'

882
01:10:30.330 --> 01:10:33.970
'was an obvious curse for me'

883
01:10:35.210 --> 01:10:36.690
'Stand up'

884
01:10:37.450 --> 01:10:38.890
'Sit down'

885
01:10:39.730 --> 01:10:41.810
'I did not say "present"'

886
01:10:42.290 --> 01:10:44.610
'In this case, you are absent'

887
01:11:12.410 --> 01:11:14.210
Mr. Panahi...

888
01:11:15.170 --> 01:11:17.290
Sorry, did I wake you?

889
01:11:18.290 --> 01:11:20.570
No, I was dozing.

890
01:11:20.810 --> 01:11:25.370
Would you like us to walk a bit,
as far as the village?

891
01:11:25.530 --> 01:11:28.210
I could make a phone call.

892
01:11:28.410 --> 01:11:32.130
I'll call the production assistant.
They've been worried since yesterday.

893
01:11:32.290 --> 01:11:34.530
I don't feel up to it.

894
01:11:35.210 --> 01:11:36.890
I'll come if you need me.

895
01:11:37.050 --> 01:11:38.410
No.

896
01:11:38.570 --> 01:11:41.970
Have a rest. I'll come back quickly.

897
01:11:42.170 --> 01:11:44.050
Enjoy yourself.

898
01:12:05.290 --> 01:12:06.770
Hello?

899
01:12:06.930 --> 01:12:09.850
Good evening, Mr. Ahmadi.
I'm really sorry.

900
01:12:10.010 --> 01:12:13.010
I know. I understand you.

901
01:12:13.450 --> 01:12:15.730
I had a serious situation.

902
01:12:15.890 --> 01:12:17.410
I don't know...

903
01:12:17.570 --> 01:12:21.770
Even if I had been on set,
I would have been useless.

904
01:12:22.970 --> 01:12:24.890
I spoke to them.

905
01:12:26.290 --> 01:12:27.490
Yes.

906
01:12:31.210 --> 01:12:35.610
I understand.
You're absolutely right.

907
01:12:35.770 --> 01:12:38.450
But you can tell me for tomorrow.

908
01:12:39.530 --> 01:12:42.770
We can shoot at night, from 6 on.

909
01:12:42.930 --> 01:12:46.330
Count me in. I'll be in Tehran.
- May I interrupt?

910
01:12:47.690 --> 01:12:51.690
Thank you.
I'll explain when I see you.

911
01:12:53.330 --> 01:12:55.770
Not at all. Nothing to do with it.

912
01:12:55.930 --> 01:12:58.050
No problem like that.

913
01:12:58.210 --> 01:13:00.130
I'll explain everything.

914
01:13:00.290 --> 01:13:02.850
Thanks for being so understanding.

915
01:13:03.370 --> 01:13:05.370
Thank you so much.

916
01:13:05.530 --> 01:13:07.890
Good evening. Bye.

917
01:13:08.210 --> 01:13:11.050
Since you're here,
how does the TV series end?

918
01:13:11.210 --> 01:13:14.810
As always: tears and mourning!

919
01:13:15.370 --> 01:13:17.850
A character will die.

920
01:13:18.450 --> 01:13:20.570
Thank you very much, sir.

921
01:13:21.970 --> 01:13:23.290
Excuse me.

922
01:13:23.450 --> 01:13:25.970
How much do I owe you?
- You're my guest.

923
01:13:26.170 --> 01:13:27.650
No, please.

924
01:13:27.810 --> 01:13:30.450
I had a tea, I was able to phone...

925
01:13:30.610 --> 01:13:32.970
Please, I'm embarrassed.

926
01:13:33.170 --> 01:13:35.450
It's nothing really.

927
01:13:35.610 --> 01:13:37.330
It's an honor to have you.

928
01:13:37.490 --> 01:13:40.890
Thank you very much. Goodbye.

929
01:13:41.090 --> 01:13:43.290
The gentleman isn't here?

930
01:13:43.450 --> 01:13:47.210
No, he's tired.
He's sleeping in the car.

931
01:13:47.370 --> 01:13:49.410
I wanted to tell him something.

932
01:13:49.570 --> 01:13:51.210
I can tell him for you.

933
01:13:51.370 --> 01:13:52.850
I don't dare tell you.

934
01:13:53.050 --> 01:13:55.170
Consider me like your daughter.

935
01:13:55.330 --> 01:13:57.850
Not here in the café.

936
01:13:58.050 --> 01:14:01.850
Let's go to my home
for a few minutes.

937
01:14:02.050 --> 01:14:04.170
Do you remember my house?

938
01:14:04.330 --> 01:14:06.690
The one with the yard?
- That's it.

939
01:14:06.850 --> 01:14:09.930
But I have to go back soon.
- Okay.

940
01:14:10.410 --> 01:14:12.330
I've got a souvenir

941
01:14:12.490 --> 01:14:15.770
for you and the gentleman.

942
01:14:15.930 --> 01:14:18.330
It's from the circumcision party.

943
01:14:18.490 --> 01:14:21.050
Thank you.
Was it for your grandson?

944
01:14:21.210 --> 01:14:22.730
Certainly not!

945
01:14:22.890 --> 01:14:24.930
My son! Not my grandson.

946
01:14:25.130 --> 01:14:27.530
Bravo, a child at your age?

947
01:14:27.690 --> 01:14:29.650
I wish you had been there.

948
01:14:29.810 --> 01:14:32.810
To see all with your own eyes.

949
01:14:32.970 --> 01:14:36.290
You wouldn't have believed
he was getting cut.

950
01:14:36.450 --> 01:14:38.290
He didn't shed a single tear.

951
01:14:39.570 --> 01:14:43.370
When my eldest Ayoub was circumcised,
I took his foreskin

952
01:14:43.530 --> 01:14:45.570
with me to Tehran.

953
01:14:46.970 --> 01:14:49.650
I wanted to bury it near a palace.

954
01:14:49.810 --> 01:14:53.570
So that one day,
my son Ayoub would work there,

955
01:14:53.730 --> 01:14:55.890
even as a janitor,

956
01:14:56.490 --> 01:14:57.970
and he could help me.

957
01:14:58.170 --> 01:15:00.890
The guards arrested me.

958
01:15:01.090 --> 01:15:04.410
They put me in jail
and beat me half to death.

959
01:15:04.570 --> 01:15:07.330
They hit me every day.

960
01:15:07.490 --> 01:15:09.970
They finally let me go.

961
01:15:10.170 --> 01:15:12.930
Then I went to the cinema.

962
01:15:13.410 --> 01:15:15.690
I saw a film,

963
01:15:15.850 --> 01:15:17.610
I left

964
01:15:17.770 --> 01:15:19.410
and went home.

965
01:15:21.130 --> 01:15:24.530
Later, God gave me four daughters.

966
01:15:24.690 --> 01:15:25.890
Congratulations.

967
01:15:26.850 --> 01:15:29.170
Even my second wife

968
01:15:29.330 --> 01:15:31.450
couldn't have a son.

969
01:15:31.610 --> 01:15:33.770
She never had a boy.

970
01:15:37.370 --> 01:15:41.210
12 years ago, God granted me a boy,

971
01:15:41.370 --> 01:15:43.970
another son.

972
01:15:48.170 --> 01:15:49.450
Good evening, ma'am.

973
01:15:49.610 --> 01:15:51.930
Sorry to have bothered you.

974
01:15:52.130 --> 01:15:53.450
Thank you very much.

975
01:15:55.730 --> 01:15:57.050
Thanks.

976
01:15:58.970 --> 01:16:01.050
How much does meat cost in Tehran?

977
01:16:01.210 --> 01:16:04.730
I don't buy meat.
I'm vegetarian.

978
01:16:05.290 --> 01:16:06.730
You were saying?

979
01:16:06.890 --> 01:16:09.050
Wait until my wife leaves.

980
01:16:15.330 --> 01:16:18.010
And what's the weather like
in Tehran?

981
01:16:18.570 --> 01:16:21.370
It's hot and polluted.

982
01:16:21.810 --> 01:16:23.570
Here, it's refreshing.

983
01:16:30.090 --> 01:16:31.210
Here you go.

984
01:16:31.410 --> 01:16:34.810
Thank you. You shouldn't have.

985
01:16:35.010 --> 01:16:36.730
Thanks.

986
01:16:36.890 --> 01:16:39.210
Don't trouble yourself.

987
01:16:39.690 --> 01:16:42.810
It's all fine, thanks.

988
01:16:59.330 --> 01:17:01.650
I was wondering...

989
01:17:02.850 --> 01:17:06.010
That story you were telling me
about your son,

990
01:17:06.490 --> 01:17:11.090
what influence could that have
on his future, his job?

991
01:17:11.410 --> 01:17:13.730
Where you're from,

992
01:17:13.890 --> 01:17:16.050
you don't circumcise boys?

993
01:17:16.210 --> 01:17:18.170
What happens to the foreskin?

994
01:17:18.730 --> 01:17:21.490
I suppose they throw it away.

995
01:17:21.650 --> 01:17:25.770
But it's sacred.
No wonder bad things happen to you.

996
01:17:25.930 --> 01:17:28.570
A boy's destiny depends on it.

997
01:17:28.730 --> 01:17:30.770
You have to give it to his godfather

998
01:17:31.170 --> 01:17:35.730
to hide in a chosen spot.

999
01:17:35.810 --> 01:17:38.170
Put it in a prison yard,

1000
01:17:38.330 --> 01:17:41.050
the boy will become a delinquent.

1001
01:17:41.210 --> 01:17:44.370
Put it in a university courtyard,

1002
01:17:44.530 --> 01:17:47.210
he'll become a doctor or engineer.

1003
01:17:47.770 --> 01:17:50.850
That's amusing.
- Nothing to laugh about.

1004
01:17:51.690 --> 01:17:54.650
I'm not laughing.

1005
01:17:54.810 --> 01:17:57.290
If you want him to be a doctor,

1006
01:17:57.450 --> 01:18:00.290
you only have to bury the thing

1007
01:18:00.690 --> 01:18:02.490
in the right place, is that it?

1008
01:18:02.650 --> 01:18:04.810
Of course not!

1009
01:18:05.010 --> 01:18:06.810
He has to go to college!

1010
01:18:07.010 --> 01:18:10.410
But if you place it correctly,
God will encourage him

1011
01:18:10.570 --> 01:18:12.850
to work really hard

1012
01:18:13.050 --> 01:18:15.090
to get into university.

1013
01:18:15.210 --> 01:18:17.770
Those are our customs.

1014
01:18:19.050 --> 01:18:21.490
Do you know Zail?

1015
01:18:21.650 --> 01:18:22.890
Who?

1016
01:18:23.210 --> 01:18:24.410
Shir Mammad.

1017
01:18:24.570 --> 01:18:28.090
Everybody knows him, but not you?

1018
01:18:28.210 --> 01:18:30.090
What is his full name?

1019
01:18:30.210 --> 01:18:31.290
Vossoughi.

1020
01:18:31.610 --> 01:18:32.770
Behrouz Vossoughi.

1021
01:18:33.970 --> 01:18:35.290
Behrouz Vossoughi?

1022
01:18:35.450 --> 01:18:37.130
Yes, look.

1023
01:18:40.570 --> 01:18:42.010
Here.

1024
01:18:42.170 --> 01:18:44.290
He's a real man.

1025
01:18:44.450 --> 01:18:46.130
He's virile.

1026
01:18:46.290 --> 01:18:48.810
He's brave.

1027
01:18:49.010 --> 01:18:53.050
You can tell from his gaze
that he's a man.

1028
01:18:53.210 --> 01:18:55.170
For sure.

1029
01:18:55.690 --> 01:18:57.610
Is he still alive?
- Yes.

1030
01:18:57.770 --> 01:18:59.370
Good.

1031
01:18:59.530 --> 01:19:01.810
I thank God.

1032
01:19:02.010 --> 01:19:03.890
As long as he lives,

1033
01:19:04.090 --> 01:19:06.170
Ayoub's fate is in his hands.

1034
01:19:06.330 --> 01:19:10.090
I've kept this for 38 years

1035
01:19:10.330 --> 01:19:14.770
to be able to guarantee him a future,
by the grace of God.

1036
01:19:17.410 --> 01:19:19.410
Could you...

1037
01:19:20.010 --> 01:19:21.010
give him this?

1038
01:19:26.370 --> 01:19:27.730
What is it?

1039
01:19:28.410 --> 01:19:30.330
Don't be offended.

1040
01:19:30.690 --> 01:19:32.330
It shouldn't repel you.

1041
01:19:32.770 --> 01:19:34.370
I've kept it in salt,

1042
01:19:34.530 --> 01:19:36.770
wrapped in cotton

1043
01:19:37.290 --> 01:19:39.330
and put it in this cloth.

1044
01:19:39.610 --> 01:19:42.210
It's my son Ayoub's foreskin.

1045
01:19:44.210 --> 01:19:45.410
What do I do with it?

1046
01:19:45.570 --> 01:19:47.210
Be kind.

1047
01:19:47.410 --> 01:19:49.170
Give it to the gentleman

1048
01:19:49.330 --> 01:19:52.130
to give to the virile man.

1049
01:19:52.810 --> 01:19:54.530
He can't.

1050
01:19:54.690 --> 01:19:56.850
Mr. Vossoughi is abroad.

1051
01:19:57.050 --> 01:19:58.410
Do us a favor.

1052
01:19:58.570 --> 01:20:01.810
When the gentleman goes abroad,
he can take it along.

1053
01:20:02.010 --> 01:20:03.850
But the gentleman...

1054
01:20:04.930 --> 01:20:07.090
can't go abroad.

1055
01:20:07.530 --> 01:20:09.450
And Mr. Vossoughi can't come here.

1056
01:20:10.530 --> 01:20:11.770
Why?

1057
01:20:13.090 --> 01:20:14.570
Because...

1058
01:20:15.450 --> 01:20:19.130
In that case,
give it to the gentleman

1059
01:20:19.410 --> 01:20:21.770
to give to your boss.

1060
01:20:21.970 --> 01:20:25.610
He can tell him my Ayoub story.

1061
01:20:25.770 --> 01:20:28.410
Maybe God will help us.

1062
01:20:28.730 --> 01:20:32.450
Even the problem of the gentleman
and the virile man

1063
01:20:32.610 --> 01:20:35.050
can be solved by a snippet of skin.

1064
01:20:35.210 --> 01:20:38.210
Okay.
- It has powers, I tell you.

1065
01:20:38.770 --> 01:20:41.290
Good night. Thank you.

1066
01:20:43.730 --> 01:20:45.330
Excuse me.

1067
01:20:45.490 --> 01:20:47.330
I wanted to say something else.

1068
01:20:47.490 --> 01:20:50.210
In the TV series,
I saw you're single.

1069
01:20:50.410 --> 01:20:54.330
We've got room here.
Stay, the weather's nice.

1070
01:20:54.490 --> 01:20:56.090
Thank you.

1071
01:20:56.610 --> 01:20:59.450
At least give the gentleman
this letter.

1072
01:20:59.610 --> 01:21:01.570
If he has a problem, it will help.

1073
01:21:01.730 --> 01:21:03.730
What is it?

1074
01:21:03.930 --> 01:21:06.130
My son Ayoub's life story.

1075
01:21:06.290 --> 01:21:08.490
Thank you.
- Goodbye.

1076
01:21:21.690 --> 01:21:24.210
Good evening.
What are you doing here?

1077
01:21:24.370 --> 01:21:27.690
I heard you were back.
- I was going to your house.

1078
01:21:27.890 --> 01:21:32.450
Any news of my daughter?
- Don't worry, she's fine.

1079
01:21:32.610 --> 01:21:35.170
You saw her with your own eyes?

1080
01:21:35.330 --> 01:21:37.810
Thank you. Let me kiss your hand.

1081
01:21:38.450 --> 01:21:39.770
You helped her a lot.

1082
01:21:39.970 --> 01:21:44.210
It's your daughter
who made me come here.

1083
01:21:44.370 --> 01:21:47.050
Good evening.
Will you come to my house?

1084
01:21:47.210 --> 01:21:49.090
Thanks, another time.

1085
01:21:49.210 --> 01:21:51.730
Don't stay in the dark.

1086
01:21:52.610 --> 01:21:55.210
Good night.

1087
01:21:55.410 --> 01:21:57.170
Thanks a lot.

1088
01:21:59.410 --> 01:22:00.890
Sleep well.

1089
01:22:01.050 --> 01:22:03.570
Your daughter is fine.
She is at Shahrzad's.

1090
01:22:07.090 --> 01:22:08.410
What's wrong?

1091
01:22:08.570 --> 01:22:10.530
Her father is coming back.

1092
01:22:11.050 --> 01:22:14.210
If her brother learns she's there,
he'll burn it down.

1093
01:22:14.410 --> 01:22:17.330
He'll burn down Shahrzad's house?

1094
01:22:17.610 --> 01:22:18.650
Why?

1095
01:22:18.810 --> 01:22:21.370
This is a village.

1096
01:22:21.530 --> 01:22:23.890
People gossip.

1097
01:22:24.170 --> 01:22:26.090
We're dishonored.

1098
01:23:32.810 --> 01:23:34.770
I thought she was in Kerman.

1099
01:23:34.970 --> 01:23:36.690
What's she doing here?

1100
01:23:36.890 --> 01:23:39.210
She came two years ago.

1101
01:23:40.170 --> 01:23:43.090
At first, they harassed her a lot.

1102
01:23:44.690 --> 01:23:48.170
When the mayor discovered
that she had appeared in films,

1103
01:23:48.330 --> 01:23:50.530
dancing,

1104
01:23:50.690 --> 01:23:53.570
he decided to chase her away.

1105
01:23:53.890 --> 01:23:56.290
He sent people

1106
01:23:56.650 --> 01:23:58.210
to...

1107
01:23:58.370 --> 01:24:01.050
to go and throw her things out.

1108
01:24:03.130 --> 01:24:05.690
That didn't bother her.

1109
01:24:05.890 --> 01:24:07.810
She painted all day long.

1110
01:24:08.010 --> 01:24:10.450
She said being outside
didn't bother her.

1111
01:24:11.930 --> 01:24:14.930
People finally left her in peace.

1112
01:24:15.330 --> 01:24:19.730
The mayor banned us
from going to her house

1113
01:24:19.930 --> 01:24:21.490
and she never visited anybody.

1114
01:24:21.930 --> 01:24:23.970
But she was all we spoke about.

1115
01:24:24.130 --> 01:24:27.890
My mother would say: "You want to be
an entertainer like Shahrzad?"

1116
01:24:28.050 --> 01:24:30.970
Are you two plotting
to trick a new victim?

1117
01:24:31.130 --> 01:24:32.210
Did you phone?

1118
01:24:32.410 --> 01:24:36.530
Yes, I have to be in Tehran
tomorrow evening at 6.

1119
01:24:36.690 --> 01:24:38.330
We'll be there.
- I hope so.

1120
01:24:38.490 --> 01:24:41.210
An old man gave me this for you.

1121
01:24:41.410 --> 01:24:43.610
What is it?
- A letter.

1122
01:24:43.770 --> 01:24:46.490
I'll explain the rest later.

1123
01:24:46.650 --> 01:24:48.410
I'm off. I'm starving.

1124
01:24:48.570 --> 01:24:51.210
I saw Marziyeh's mother.

1125
01:24:51.370 --> 01:24:52.930
Good night.

1126
01:25:01.570 --> 01:25:03.890
Please open that later.

1127
01:25:04.050 --> 01:25:05.170
What?

1128
01:25:05.330 --> 01:25:06.930
Open it later.

1129
01:25:08.410 --> 01:25:10.330
You know what it is?

1130
01:25:13.050 --> 01:25:14.490
They are all together.

1131
01:25:29.650 --> 01:25:31.330
Any news from your fiancé?

1132
01:25:31.570 --> 01:25:33.810
Why don't we hear about him?

1133
01:25:34.410 --> 01:25:36.890
He's been a deserter for five years.

1134
01:25:37.050 --> 01:25:39.490
From time to time, he breaks down

1135
01:25:39.650 --> 01:25:41.370
and returns to the village.

1136
01:25:41.530 --> 01:25:43.690
He stays a while,

1137
01:25:43.890 --> 01:25:46.890
then decides to leave again.

1138
01:25:47.050 --> 01:25:50.290
Each time he promises
not to desert again,

1139
01:25:51.530 --> 01:25:53.490
but he does what he likes.

1140
01:25:53.650 --> 01:25:55.690
He could show up anytime.

1141
01:25:56.130 --> 01:25:57.530
What would you do then?

1142
01:25:57.690 --> 01:26:01.370
I have no problem convincing him.

1143
01:26:01.890 --> 01:26:03.930
His family is another matter.

1144
01:26:04.370 --> 01:26:08.170
There's no logic, no rules here.
Except for the road.

1145
01:26:08.330 --> 01:26:12.970
But they change them everyday,
instead of repairing the road.

1146
01:26:13.370 --> 01:26:15.930
One day, I took a spade and pick

1147
01:26:15.970 --> 01:26:18.570
to go and widen some of the road,

1148
01:26:18.730 --> 01:26:21.730
so that two cars could pass.

1149
01:26:21.930 --> 01:26:25.490
They took away the spade:
"That's not for women."

1150
01:26:25.650 --> 01:26:28.370
"These tools represent
the farmer's honor."

1151
01:26:30.930 --> 01:26:33.370
Can you switch it off? Sorry.

1152
01:26:35.930 --> 01:26:37.330
Take this.

1153
01:26:47.090 --> 01:26:48.050
Good evening.

1154
01:26:48.610 --> 01:26:50.490
What brings you here?

1155
01:26:50.970 --> 01:26:53.890
How are you?

1156
01:26:55.170 --> 01:26:58.050
Fine, thanks.

1157
01:26:58.530 --> 01:27:00.570
And you?

1158
01:27:00.730 --> 01:27:01.930
Come to our home.

1159
01:27:02.090 --> 01:27:06.330
The mayor asked us
to treat you like a guest.

1160
01:27:06.490 --> 01:27:09.570
Thanks a lot. We're leaving at dawn.

1161
01:27:09.730 --> 01:27:14.010
That's why I'm staying here.
Otherwise I would come. Thanks.

1162
01:27:14.170 --> 01:27:15.290
Do you need anything?

1163
01:27:15.450 --> 01:27:18.650
No, I've got everything.
Otherwise I'd bother you.

1164
01:27:18.850 --> 01:27:21.010
Clothing, a blanket?

1165
01:27:21.170 --> 01:27:23.490
That's kind, but no thanks.

1166
01:27:25.970 --> 01:27:28.410
Thanks a lot.

1167
01:27:29.170 --> 01:27:30.730
Give everyone my regards.

1168
01:27:30.930 --> 01:27:33.250
We won't disturb you any longer.

1169
01:27:33.410 --> 01:27:36.010
Thank you very much. Good evening.

1170
01:27:36.170 --> 01:27:39.330
Good evening. Take care.

1171
01:27:42.650 --> 01:27:45.290
City folks never listen.

1172
01:27:45.450 --> 01:27:50.490
A strong hailstorm would show him.

1173
01:27:51.450 --> 01:27:53.490
Careful what you say.

1174
01:27:53.650 --> 01:27:55.450
That's worse for us.

1175
01:27:56.210 --> 01:27:59.690
We would lose all our crops.

1176
01:28:03.690 --> 01:28:06.450
Even so, it would teach him a lesson.

1177
01:29:22.090 --> 01:29:23.010
Good morning.

1178
01:29:24.890 --> 01:29:27.090
Did you sleep well?

1179
01:29:27.250 --> 01:29:30.330
Do you want to wash your face?

1180
01:29:31.610 --> 01:29:32.570
Good morning.

1181
01:29:38.650 --> 01:29:42.490
At dawn, she went out
with her painting gear.

1182
01:29:44.850 --> 01:29:46.890
She left you a gift.

1183
01:30:04.210 --> 01:30:06.610
She doesn't resent me too much.

1184
01:30:07.250 --> 01:30:09.170
No, she lives her life.

1185
01:30:11.050 --> 01:30:13.290
And what's this?

1186
01:30:15.290 --> 01:30:17.010
I'm now a godfather.

1187
01:30:18.490 --> 01:30:20.770
I'll put it here, don't forget.

1188
01:30:24.090 --> 01:30:25.370
Shall we go?

1189
01:32:00.290 --> 01:32:01.210
Mr. Panahi...

1190
01:32:01.370 --> 01:32:05.090
Women know better
how to handle these situations.

1191
01:32:16.050 --> 01:32:17.330
Who is it?

1192
01:32:18.090 --> 01:32:19.450
Good morning.

1193
01:32:19.610 --> 01:32:20.890
Who's there?

1194
01:32:21.810 --> 01:32:23.410
It's us.

1195
01:32:26.970 --> 01:32:29.770
I've brought Marziyeh back.

1196
01:32:30.610 --> 01:32:33.250
Come in.
- Thanks.

1197
01:32:34.170 --> 01:32:36.570
Promise me there will be no trouble.

1198
01:32:36.770 --> 01:32:38.410
Come in.

1199
01:32:58.210 --> 01:33:01.010
Get out.

1200
01:33:01.170 --> 01:33:03.570
Where do you want me to go?

1201
01:33:06.730 --> 01:33:08.770
Open the door.

1202
01:36:07.810 --> 01:36:10.090
I'll walk for a bit.

1203
01:38:08.570 --> 01:38:10.210
Madam Jafari!

1204
01:38:10.370 --> 01:38:12.890
Madam Jafari, wait for me!
